  "body": "Seen twice on 2026-11-12. A batch gate was running in the main checkout (the law: \"the gate runs there ... reusing its target/\") when `git pull --ff-only origin main` moved that checkout to a newer commit mid-run (reflog: 11:47 and 13:32 local). Cargo then compiled whatever was on disk at each step: the first time the last step failed to build new UI sources against old libraries; the second time the gate printed 9/9 ok for a mix of 2d13cf44 and d7e9a807. Neither run is a valid result for any commit, and each cost about 30 minutes of machine time.\n\n**Cause.** Not a person: the pulls match the start-up of issue workers. AGENTS.md \"Start from the latest main\" gives two forms - `git fetch origin && git switch main && git pull --ff-only origin main` and, for a worktree agent, `git fetch origin && git worktree add --no-track -b issue/N-<slug> .claude/worktrees/issue-N origin/main` - and the work-issue skill does not forbid the first form to a worker that then makes a worktree anyway. Nothing tells a worker that the main checkout may be busy, and `cargo xtask gate` does not notice the tree changing under it.\n\n**Wanted**\n1. AGENTS.md and the `work-issue` skill: an agent that works in a worktree NEVER switches, pulls, merges or resets in the main checkout - `git fetch origin` and `git worktree add ... origin/main` only. Say why (the main checkout may be running a gate).\n2. `cargo xtask gate` (every tier): record `HEAD` and a tree fingerprint at the start; check them again before each step and at the end; if they changed, stop and exit non-zero with \"the checkout moved from <a> to <b> during the gate - this run is void\", never a green summary.\n3. Optional, decide: the gate takes a lock while it runs (e.g. `.claude/gate-running.lock`, gitignored) and a `reference-transaction` hook installed by `cargo xtask` refuses to move the local `main` while the lock exists. The orchestrating session installed exactly that by hand in the maintainer's clone on 2026-11-12 (`.git/hooks/reference-transaction`, local only); if it proves itself, ship it through xtask so every clone has it; if not, remove the hand-made one.\n\nDone means: a worker brief cannot lead to a pull in the main checkout (skill text, pinned by the skill's eval if it has one for start-up); a gate whose checkout moved mid-run fails loudly (xtask unit test with a fake HEAD change); `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` bumped and announced on #681.\n",
